{"H4800":{"lemma":"מֶרְחָב","xlit":"merchâb","gloss":"breadth, large place (room).","def":"enlargement, either literally (an open space, usually in a good sense), or figuratively (liberty)"},"H4801":{"lemma":"מֶרְחָק","xlit":"merchâq","gloss":"(a-, dwell in, very) far (country, off). See also H1023 (בֵּית הַמֶּרְחָק).","def":"remoteness, i.e. (concretely) a distant place; often (adverbially) from afar"},"H4802":{"lemma":"מַרְחֶשֶׁת","xlit":"marchesheth","gloss":"fryingpan.","def":"a stewpan"},"H4803":{"lemma":"מָרַט","xlit":"mâraṭ","gloss":"bright, furbish, (have his) hair (be) fallen off, peeled, pluck off (hair).","def":"to polish; by implication, to make bald (the head), to gall (the shoulder); also, to sharpen"},"H4804":{"lemma":"מְרַט","xlit":"mᵉraṭ","gloss":"be plucked.","def":"to pull off"},"H4805":{"lemma":"מְרִי","xlit":"mᵉrîy","gloss":"bitter, (most) rebel(-lion, -lious).","def":"bitterness, i.e. (figuratively) rebellion; concretely, bitter, or rebellious"},"H4806":{"lemma":"מְרִיא","xlit":"mᵉrîyʼ","gloss":"fat (fed) beast (cattle, -ling).","def":"stall-fed; often (as noun) a beeve"},"H4807":{"lemma":"מְרִיב בַּעַל","xlit":"Mᵉrîyb Baʻal","gloss":"Merib-baal. Compare H4810 (מְרִי בַעַל).","def":"quarreller of Baal, Merib-Baal, an epithet of Gideon"},"H4808":{"lemma":"מְרִיבָה","xlit":"mᵉrîybâh","gloss":"provocation, strife.","def":"quarrel"},"H4809":{"lemma":"מְרִיבָה","xlit":"Mᵉrîybâh","gloss":"Meribah.","def":"Meribah, the name of two places in the Desert"},"H4810":{"lemma":"מְרִי בַעַל","xlit":"Mᵉrîy Baʻal","gloss":"Meri-baal. Compare H4807 (מְרִיב בַּעַל).","def":"Meri-Baal, an epithet of Gideon"},"H4811":{"lemma":"מְרָיָה","xlit":"Mᵉrâyâh","gloss":"Meraiah. Compare H3236 (יִמְרָה).","def":"Merajah, an Israelite"},"H4812":{"lemma":"מְרָיוֹת","xlit":"Mᵉrâyôwth","gloss":"Meraioth.","def":"Merajoth, the name of two Israelites"},"H4813":{"lemma":"מִרְיָם","xlit":"Miryâm","gloss":"Miriam.","def":"Mirjam, the name of two Israelitesses"},"H4814":{"lemma":"מְרִ