lace in Palestine"},"H4832":{"lemma":"מַרְפֵּא","xlit":"marpêʼ","gloss":"(in-)cure(-able), healing(-lth), remedy, sound, wholesome, yielding.","def":"properly, curative, i.e. literally (concretely) a medicine, or (abstractly) a cure; figuratively (concretely) deliverance, or (abstractly) placidity"},"H4833":{"lemma":"מִרְפָּשׂ","xlit":"mirpâs","gloss":"that which...have fouled.","def":"muddled water"},"H4834":{"lemma":"מָרַץ","xlit":"mârats","gloss":"embolden, be forcible, grievous, sore.","def":"properly, to press, i.e. (figuratively) to be pungent or vehement; to irritate"},"H4835":{"lemma":"מְרֻצָה","xlit":"mᵉrutsâh","gloss":"violence. See also H4794 (מְרוּצָה).","def":"oppression"},"H4836":{"lemma":"מַרְצֵעַ","xlit":"martsêaʻ","gloss":"aul.","def":"an awl"},"H4837":{"lemma":"מַרְצֶפֶת","xlit":"martsepheth","gloss":"pavement.","def":"a pavement"},"H4838":{"lemma":"מָרַק","xlit":"mâraq","gloss":"bright, furbish, scour.","def":"to polish; by implication, to sharpen; also to rinse"},"H4839":{"lemma":"מָרָק","xlit":"mârâq","gloss":"broth. See also H6564 (פָּרָק).","def":"soup (as if a rinsing)"},"H4840":{"lemma":"מֶרְקָח","xlit":"merqâch","gloss":"[idiom] sweet.","def":"a spicy herb"},"H4841":{"lemma":"מֶרְקָחָה","xlit":"merqâchâh","gloss":"pot of ointment, [idiom] well.","def":"abstractly, a seasoning (with spicery); concretely, an unguentkettle (for preparing spiced oil)"},"H4842":{"lemma":"מִרְקַחַת","xlit":"mirqachath","gloss":"prepared by the apothecaries' art, compound, ointment.","def":"an aromatic unguent; also an unguent-pot"},"H4843":{"lemma":"מָרַר","xlit":"mârar","gloss":"(be, be in, deal, have, make) bitter(-ly, -ness), be moved with choler, (be, have sorely, it) grieved(-eth), provoke, vex.","def":"to be (causatively, make) bitter (literally or figuratively)"},"H4844":{"lemma":"מְרֹר","xlit":"mᵉrôr","gloss":"bitter(-ness).","def":"a bitter herb"},"H4845":{"lemma":"מְרֵרָה","xlit":"mᵉrêrâh","gloss":"gall.","def":"bile (from its bitterness)"},"H4846":{"le